{"id":"chatcmpl-28b0d34d-8400-4677-a31d-1fa80bebbd2d","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246370,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task succeeded by using multiple independent expert models to cross-check a laterality-sensitive radiological finding before committing to an answer. The key insight is that ambiguous spatial/laterality judgments benefit from redundant verification across tools, and that lateral-view anatomy requires explicit reasoning about which hemidiaphragm is affected. The pattern generalizes to any visual QA task where side-specific findings must be localized.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a finding is laterality-sensitive (left vs right), query multiple independent expert tools and require agreement before answering.\",\n    \"For lateral-view or non-standard projections, explicitly ask the tool to reason about anatomical landmarks (e.g., which hemidiaphragm) rather than just presence/absence.\",\n    \"Decompose the diagnostic question into sub-questions (presence, then laterality) and route each to the most appropriate specialized tool.\",\n    \"Use cross-model consensus as a confidence signal: converging independent outputs justify a definitive answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Route presence-detection and laterality/localization to separate expert calls; require agreement across at least two independent models before finalizing.\",\n    \"Visual question answering with side-specific options\": \"Explicitly ask tools to name the affected side using anatomical landmarks, not just confirm the abnormality exists.\",\n    \"Multi-tool consensus tasks\": \"Design calls so each tool independently addresses the same sub-question; treat agreement as validation and disagreement as a trigger for further probing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's presence first, then separately confirm its laterality/location before selecting an option.\",\n    \"Verify that at least two independent tools agree on the side-specific conclusion before releasing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":512,"total_tokens":877,"completion_tokens":365,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":512},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":365}}}